# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vivado / SDK files are generated, so in general they are not tracked.
# Exception (18 Oct 2026): the ZedBoard project mac_attack_accel/zed/mac_zed_project IS tracked,
# with its block design, its results (bitstream, checkpoints, reports) and its SDK projects, so
# a teammate can open it, program the board and run the app without the 20-minute build.
# zed/create_zed_project.tcl still rebuilds the project from scratch if it ever breaks.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Vivado generated (no path prefix, so it matches at any depth)
mac_attack_project/
.Xil/
*.cache/
*.runs/
*.sim/
*.hw/
*.gen/
*.ip_user_files/
vivado*.jou
vivado*.log
vivado*.str
webtalk*
*.wdb

# Xilinx SDK / hardware exports: keep only the SDK application projects (MAC_*)
**/*.sdk/*
!**/*.sdk/MAC_*/
**/*.sdk/*_bsp/
**/*.sdk/MAC_*/Debug/
**/*.sdk/MAC_*/Release/
*.hdf
*.bit

# The ZedBoard project, tracked (see the top). These lines must stay below the general rules.
# Tracked: mac_zed.xpr, mac_zed.srcs (block design and IP), mac_zed.runs (bitstream, checkpoints,
# reports), mac_zed.hw, and in mac_zed.sdk the .hdf, the hardware platform, the BSP and the apps.
# Still not tracked: .cache, .sim, .ip_user_files, .Xil, logs/journals, the SDK workspace settings
# (.metadata) and the apps' Debug/Release build folders (the tools remake all of these).
!**/mac_zed_project/mac_zed.runs/
!**/mac_zed_project/mac_zed.hw/
!**/mac_zed_project/**/*.bit
!**/mac_zed_project/**/*.hdf
!**/mac_zed_project/mac_zed.sdk/*
**/mac_zed_project/mac_zed.sdk/.metadata/
**/mac_zed_project/mac_zed.sdk/RemoteSystemsTempFiles/
**/mac_zed_project/mac_zed.sdk/webtalk/
**/mac_zed_project/mac_zed.sdk/.sdk/
**/mac_zed_project/mac_zed.sdk/*/Debug/
**/mac_zed_project/mac_zed.sdk/*/Release/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Large data
*.wav
data/

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
